The Windows resource monitor bundles LibreHardwareMonitorLib 0.9.6 and its
NuGet dependencies, with a self-contained .NET runtime. See
web/native/NOTICE.md and the adapter's licenses/ directory for source,
versions and license notices.

The Linux resource monitor bundles LibreHardwareMonitor-Linux 1.2.0,
Copyright 2026 Insight-IT GmbH, Berlin — Dominic Ballenthin, under the MIT
License, with a private CPython runtime. See web/native/linux/vendor/LICENSE,
web/native/linux/vendor/UPSTREAM.json and web/native/NOTICE.md for source,
versions and runtime notices. macOS uses native OS readers.

Remote Desktop (screen mirroring) is built from MoonlightWeb
(https://github.com/linckosz/moonlight-web), Copyright 2026 Bruno Martin,
licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later: its capture,
encoding and streaming engine in web/native/screen (built into the
sfagents-screen helper, which SF Agents downloads from this repository's
releases) and its stream page in web/public/screen. Both are changed for
SF Agents; web/native/screen/UPSTREAM.json and web/public/screen/UPSTREAM.json
name the commit and every change. The helper's archive includes Qt
(LGPL-3.0), libdatachannel (MPL-2.0), OpenSSL (Apache-2.0), Opus and OpenH264
(BSD) and the virtual display driver (MIT) MoonlightWeb uses. On Windows, the
startup approval also installs ViGEmBus (BSD-3-Clause), downloaded from its
official release, for gamepads.

Dictation downloads, on first use, a llama.cpp release
(https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp, MIT License) and Qwen3-ASR-1.7B in
unsloth's GGUF conversion (https://huggingface.co/unslothai/Qwen3-ASR-1.7B-GGUF,
Apache License 2.0). Neither is included in SF Agents.
